      "basis": "The document's own copyright paragraph, under its header: \"Copyright © 2018 W3C® (MIT, ERCIM, Keio, Beihang). W3C liability, trademark and permissive document license rules apply\", where 'permissive document license' links to https://www.w3.org/Consortium/Legal/2015/copyright-software-and-document (the W3C Software and Document License, SPDX W3C-20150513). That licence permits copying, modifying and distributing the work provided the notice, any pre-existing notices, and a statement of changes go with every copy; the notice is in `note`, so this entry holds the text in full (issue #1614).",
      "note": "Source: the W3C Working Group's own publication snapshot of the Recommendation, github.com/w3c/poe at commit e3a45ad650e370c9c520520a5c759fce3bb2075e, path snapshots/REC-odrl-model-20180215/index.html (last changed there in a448083a794b89fd08b6d7ae41ff7503c71385a6, 2018-02-09). Its status section and header read 'W3C Recommendation 15 February 2018', 'This version: https://www.w3.org/TR/2018/REC-odrl-model-20180215/'. It is therefore the REC text as the WG staged it for publication, NOT an editor's draft; w3.org is unreachable from the ingesting container, so it was not compared byte for byte with the copy at https://www.w3.org/TR/2018/REC-odrl-model-20180215/. Printed to PDF offline (headless Chromium 141, network blocked, document outline from the headings), then ingested with the pdf-structure rung. Styles and the W3C logo, which load from w3.org, are absent from the print; the text and the repository-local figures are not. Errata published after the REC are not included. NOTICE: This entry includes material copied from or derived from ODRL Information Model 2.2, https://www.w3.org/TR/2018/REC-odrl-model-20180215/. Copyright © 2018 W3C® (MIT, ERCIM, Keio, Beihang). Licensed under the W3C Software and Document License, https://www.w3.org/Consortium/Legal/2015/copyright-software-and-document. Changes: the HTML was printed to PDF and its text split into one Markdown file per outline section; the wording is unchanged."
